# DealerDesk

- Behavioural truth: `docs/SYSTEM.md` and the C sources. Prefer code and
  `data/*.dat` over `README.md` when they conflict.
- Pricing truth: `calc.c` (`calc_quote`).
- Do not invent code, features, or behaviour the ticket did not ask for.
- Docs, comments, commits, and rules: English.
- Global project rule: never add git commit trailers (`Co-authored-by`,
  `Signed-off-by`, `Generated-by`, `Assisted-by`, `Made-with`, or equivalents).
  Not optional. Authorship is the human owner only.
- No push/PR unless the user asks. No force-push unless explicitly requested.
- Delivery workstream (`docs/TASKS.md`): one commit per completed todo; append
  `docs/JOURNAL.md` (date, phase, task id, SHA, note). Outside that workstream,
  do not commit unless the user asks.
- Challenge ground rules live in `AGENTS.md` (AI expected, stack free, staff
  must not notice non-ticket changes, commit as you go, ambiguity → write down).
- Trusted quality: Docker + CTest/TDD (+ Docker pre-run gate). Multi-OS GitHub
  Release binaries are CI/CD demo only: no sanity suite on those artifacts;
  out-of-Docker use is user discretion.
- Gherkin under `features/` = behaviour/acceptance contract, not implementation
  spec. CTest verifies. No Gherkin runner unless explicitly added.
- SDLC: `docs/SDLC.md`. BDD then TDD are mandatory on every behaviour change.
- Canonical agent instructions: `AGENTS.md` (shared with Claude, Copilot,
  DeepSeek, and other agents via their entry files).
- Agents draft scenarios/tests/code; humans decide and always run manual checks.
- Prefer Docker + CMake/CTest when present; legacy: `gcc -o dealerdesk *.c -lm`
  from repo root.
- Preserve existing quote/invoice totals for non-ticket paths (to the penny).
- Do not open a PR against the upstream original challenge repository.
